course: dictionary
lesson: 831
title: One word, two animals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around it, shows which meaning the writer intends. «The beluga lives in the Arctic, where its white skin hides it among the ice.» The clues Arctic and ice tell you that here a beluga is a white whale.
explain: Now read «The beluga sturgeon can live over 100 years and grow longer than a car.» A sturgeon is a fish, so here a beluga is a very large fish. It is the same word, but the clues show you which animal is meant.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does "a white whale" still make sense in the sturgeon sentence? No, so the meaning there must be the fish.
fact: A beluga whale is a white whale of the Arctic with a round head and no back fin.
fact: Belugas are sometimes called «sea canaries» because they whistle, click and chirp.
fact: A beluga can change the shape of its melon, the rounded part of its forehead, to aim its clicks.
fact: Belugas use echoes to find food and breathing holes in the ice. This is called echolocation.
fact: A beluga is also a very large fish, a kind of sturgeon, whose eggs are sold as expensive caviar.
exercise: «The beluga lives in the Arctic, where its white skin hides it among the ice.» In this sentence, what is a beluga? | *A white whale of the Arctic | A large fish with expensive eggs | A dinosaur that lived on ice | A kind of bird
exercise: «The beluga sturgeon can live over 100 years.» What kind of animal is the beluga here? | A whale with a round head | *A very large fish | A seal from the Arctic | A bird that whistles
exercise: Why are belugas called «sea canaries»? | They sing in a choir | *They whistle, click and chirp | They are yellow and fly over the sea | They eat seeds from plants
test: What do belugas use echoes for? | To grow a back fin | To hide from the sun | *To find their food and breathing holes in the ice | To paint their skin white
test: Belugas have necks whose bones are not joined. What can a beluga do because of this? | Fly short distances over the ice | *Turn its head | Hold its breath for a whole day | Swim backwards without moving its tail
exam: Which sentence shows that the beluga is the fish, not the whale? | *«The beluga sturgeon can live over 100 years and grow longer than a car.» | «Belugas are white Arctic whales that whistle and chirp.» | «The beluga lives in the Arctic, where its white skin hides it among the ice.»
